# LIFX Lighting Schedule
# Supercronic logs all output to stdout/stderr automatically
# Times run in the TZ configured in .env
#
# Crontab entries call lifx.py directly. Jobs on the same minute run in
# parallel, so put lights that change together on one line - repeat --label
# for lights sharing values, and chain lights with different values with `;`.
#
# Use --verify on scheduled jobs: it rediscovers missing lights, reads state
# back, and retries until the lights match (exit code non-zero if they don't).
#
# Examples (uncomment / edit to build the schedule):
#
# Evening: turn on (if off) and set warm white, fading in over 2s
# 0 18 * * * lifx.py set --label "Office" --label "Desk" --saturation 0 --brightness 45875 --kelvin 3000 --duration 2000 --on --verify
#
# Late night: dim without --on, so lights someone turned off stay off
# 0 21 * * * lifx.py set --label "Office" --brightness 13107 --duration 2000 --verify; lifx.py set --label "Desk" --brightness 6554 --duration 2000 --verify
#
# Morning: power off
# 0 7 * * * lifx.py off --label "Office" --label "Desk" --duration 1000 --verify
